{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/prf-ugb-main","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:ugb-main","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of the main theorem","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/thm-ugb-main","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/lem-ugb-generator-choice","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-remainder-modules"],"tags":["groebner-basis","freeness"],"text":"ugb-main-theorem-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:ugb-main\"></a><p><em>Proof of <a href=\"#thm:ugb-main\">Theorem 2</a>.</em> Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> be an element of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>. The\ndivision algorithm allows us to write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f = r + \\tilde{f}</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\in O(I)</code> and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{f} \\in I</code>. By <a href=\"#lem:ugb-generator-choice\">Lemma 6</a> we can take\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\in \\widetilde{O}(G)</code>. As <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> is arbitrary, we have:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">A = I + \\widetilde{O}(G)</code></pre>\n<p>It remains to show that this sum is direct, which follows from uniqueness of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code>.\nSuppose the algorithm produces two representations:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">f = \\tilde{f} + r = \\tilde{f}' + r'</code></pre>\n<p>Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\tilde{f} - \\tilde{f}' \\in I</code> so that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r - r' \\in I</code>. If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r - r' \\neq 0</code>,\nthen <a href=\"#lem:ugb-generator-choice\">Lemma 6</a> shows there is some <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g_\\gamma \\in G</code>\nwith <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\LT(g_\\gamma) \\mid (r - r')</code>. But by construction of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r'</code>, no such\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g_\\gamma</code> exists — a contradiction. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/ugb-main-theorem-proof.md","heading":"Proof"}
